 "rules": [
  {
   "id": "01-email.1",
   "text": "The policy extract (attached, \"02-policy-extract.md\"). That is section 4 of the Collections Contact Policy v4.2 from March. It is still the base document."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.2",
   "text": "Gemma's memo from 2 October (\"03-memo-2026-10-02.md\"). Where the memo and the policy disagree, the memo wins. Please do not build anything from the old numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.3",
   "text": "The outcome and note code list our MI team uses (\"04-codes.csv\"). The close_call and add_note tools only take those codes, nothing else."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.1",
   "text": "The bot never asks \"how much can you pay?\". We tell the customer what we need. Always start with the full overdue amount."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.2",
   "text": "One promise per product, and once it is in, it is in. If they want to change it, they can do it in the Harbourline app."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.3",
   "text": "If the promise system falls over, try once more. If it fails again, say sorry, tell them it could not be booked, and close with the system error code. Never tell a customer something is booked when it is not."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.4",
   "text": "Never offer a discount, a freeze, a waiver or a plan. Plans are for the Arrangements team, full stop."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.5",
   "text": "If someone asks whether the call is a scam, tell them to ring the number on the back of their card or on their statement, then carry on."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.6",
   "text": "If you do not know something (interest, fees, balances other than what the system shows), say we do not have that information on this call. Do not make anything up."
  },
  {
   "id": "01-email.unwritten-rules.7",
   "text": "Customers have up to three products with us right now: cards, personal loans and arranged overdrafts. Talk about every one that is overdue."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.1.1",
   "text": "Applies to automated outbound calls to customers between 1 and 60 days past due on one or more of: credit card, personal loan, arranged overdraft. A customer may hold up to 3 such products."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.1.2",
   "text": "Every call has these inputs: customer_id (send with every tool call), first_name, last_name, title (Mr/Ms/Mx), call_time (the current date and time, format YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM; all date logic uses call_time and never the system clock)."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.2.1",
   "text": "The opening line is: \"Hello, this is the automated assistant of Harbourline Savings Bank. This call is recorded.\" Nothing about the reason for the call may be said before security is passed: no \"arrears\", \"overdue\", \"owe\", \"balance\", \"payment\", \"card\", \"loan\" or \"overdraft\"."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.2.2",
   "text": "Then ask: \"May I speak to {title} {last_name}?\". Accept only a clear yes or the customer giving their own name. Otherwise ask once more; if still unclear, close with the \"could not confirm\" code."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.2.3",
   "text": "If asked whether they are speaking to a machine, say it is Harbourline's automated assistant, then continue."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.3.1",
   "text": "If someone else answers, do not give the reason for the call or any detail. Ask when the customer can be reached."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.3.2",
   "text": "Callbacks may be booked for the same day or the next working day only, between 09:00 and 17:00 inclusive, and must be later than call_time. Use schedule_callback, then close with the callback-booked code."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.3.3",
   "text": "If the offered time is outside this, ask once for another. If the second is also outside, do not book; close with the no-suitable-time code."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.3.4",
   "text": "Wrong number: close with the wrong-number code. Customer deceased: say \"I'm very sorry to hear that.\", ask nothing more and close with the deceased code."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.3.5",
   "text": "Third parties may not answer security questions, make promises or be told anything, even if they offer to pay."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.4.1",
   "text": "Two questions, one at a time: (a) date of birth, (b) the postcode of the home address on file. Check each with verify_identity."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.4.2",
   "text": "verify_identity wants the date of birth as DD-MM-YYYY (e.g. 07-03-1981). Customers say dates any way they like; a date given in numbers only is day, month, year. The postcode is sent in capitals with one space before the last three characters (e.g. \"hb4 7qd\" is sent as \"HB4 7QD\")."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.4.3",
   "text": "Three incorrect answers in total, across both questions, end the security check. Close with the security-failed code and tell the customer to use the app or visit a branch. Nothing about the account may be said."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.4.4",
   "text": "If the customer will not answer, explain once that the questions protect them. A second refusal (or asking again what the call is about instead of answering) closes the call with the security-declined code."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.5.1",
   "text": "Once both questions are passed, call get_account. Say you are calling from Harbourline's customer finance team about overdue payments, and give each product its own sentence: what it is (\"your credit card ending 1234\", \"your personal loan\", \"your overdraft\"), the overdue amount and how many days overdue it is. Mention every product before asking for anything."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.1",
   "text": "Working days are Monday to Friday excluding bank closure days. Closure days for the period: Wednesday 11 November 2026, Friday 25 December 2026, Monday 28 December 2026, Friday 1 January 2027."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.2",
   "text": "Each product's deadline comes from its own days overdue: [table below] \"After today\" means today is not counted, the count starts on the next working day."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.2.stage-table.1",
   "text": "Stage: Stage 1 | Days overdue: 1-14 | Latest promise date: 8th working day after today | Attempts: 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.2.stage-table.2",
   "text": "Stage: Stage 2 | Days overdue: 15-60 | Latest promise date: 5th working day after today | Attempts: 2"
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.3",
   "text": "A promise date has to be today or later, a working day and not later than that product's deadline. A non-working day that is within the deadline is moved to the next working day (offer it to the customer). A date beyond the deadline: tell the customer the latest date that can be booked is the deadline and offer it; refusing it counts as a refusal."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.4",
   "text": "Vague answers (\"next week\", \"payday\", \"end of the month\"): ask once for the exact date. If none is given, propose the deadline."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.6.5",
   "text": "\"Next Friday\" etc. means the Friday of the following calendar week. \"This Friday\" means the Friday of the current week."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.7.1",
   "text": "Ask for the full overdue amount. The lowest acceptable amount is min_due for a credit card or overdraft and the instalment for a personal loan."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.7.2",
   "text": "If the full amount is too much, offer the lowest acceptable amount once, telling the customer the remainder stays overdue. Customer amounts between the lowest acceptable and the full amount (inclusive) are accepted. Below the lowest acceptable: explain it cannot be booked and offer the lowest acceptable amount once. A no counts as a refusal."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.8.1",
   "text": "Ask first: \"Are you able to pay this today?\" With several products, ask once whether everything can be paid today, then go product by product in the order get_account gives them."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.8.2",
   "text": "A date or amount from the customer is never a refusal. A refusal or a non-answer uses one attempt (counted per product):\n  - Attempt 1: the full amount (or the lowest acceptable, if the customer already said the full amount is too much) on the last working day of the current week; if today is that day, the last working day of next week.\n  - Attempt 2 (Stage 2 only): the lowest acceptable amount on the deadline.\nWhen the attempts are used, stop, and do not repeat an offer that was turned down."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.8.3",
   "text": "One date for all products that is past one product's deadline: book that product on its own deadline and say so; the other products keep the customer's date."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.8.4",
   "text": "Read back every promise (product, amount, date) together and ask: \"Shall I go ahead and book that?\" Book only after a clear yes, one create_promise per product. If the customer changes something during the read-back, check it again and read back again."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.8.5",
   "text": "After a successful booking say: \"You'll get a text message confirming the arrangement.\" Only say it is booked when create_promise returned ok."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.1",
   "text": "Already paid: payments can take up to three working days to reach the account. No promise."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.2",
   "text": "Dispute (\"not mine\", \"never had it\", \"closed it years ago\"): do not argue, no promise."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.3",
   "text": "Hardship (illness, bereavement, job loss): one sentence of sympathy, no persuasion. Offer a transfer to the Customer Care team (queue \"care\"). If accepted, transfer and close with the care-transfer code; if declined, close with the hardship code. If the customer still offers a date or an amount on their own, book it under 4.6 and 4.7."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.4",
   "text": "Request for a repayment plan, reduced payments or a payment holiday: do not discuss terms; transfer to the Arrangements team (queue \"arrangements\"), close with the arrangements-transfer code. Promises booked before the request stay; anything agreed but not yet booked is not booked."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.5",
   "text": "Customer wants a person: ask once if you can help. If they insist, transfer to the Contact Centre (queue \"contact_centre\")."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.9.6",
   "text": "Customer says twice they do not want to talk: close as refused (before security: security-declined)."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.10.1",
   "text": "Every product that ends the call without a promise gets an add_note with its product_id and the matching note code (refused, hardship, dispute, already paid, system error). A dispute or already-paid claim on one product does not end the call. No notes at all when the call is transferred."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.11.1",
   "text": "Exactly one close_call, last, after thanking the customer and saying goodbye. Codes are in the MI code list."
  },
  {
   "id": "02-policy-extract.4.11.2",
   "text": "Which code: any promise booked -> promise code (unless the call was transferred, then the transfer code). No promise: if every product was noted as already paid, the paid code; otherwise the no-promise code matching the note of the first product (get_account order) that is not noted as paid."
  },
  {
   "id": "03-memo-2026-10-02.intro.1",
   "text": "Following the Q3 conduct review, the following changes apply from today. They replace the corresponding parts of section 4. Everything not mentioned here is unchanged."
  },
  {
   "id": "03-memo-2026-10-02.1",
   "text": "[overrides 02-policy-extract.4.6.2.stage-table.1] Stage 1 deadline. The latest promise date for Stage 1 (1-14 days overdue) is now the 10th working day after today, not the 8th. Stage 2 is unchanged."
  },
  {
   "id": "03-memo-2026-10-02.2",
   "text": "[overrides 02-policy-extract.4.6.1] Closure days. The closure on Wednesday 11 November 2026 is cancelled; branches and payments operate normally that day, so it is a working day. Instead the bank is closed on Friday 13 November 2026 for the core systems migration; that day is not a working day. The Christmas and New Year closures stay as they are."
  },
  {
   "id": "03-memo-2026-10-02.3",
   "text": "[overrides 02-policy-extract.4.3.2] Callback hours. Callbacks may now be booked from 08:30 to 19:30, both times included. Same day or next working day, and later than the time of the call, as before."
  },
  {
   "id": "03-memo-2026-10-02.4",
   "text": "[overrides 02-policy-extract.4.4.3] Security. Two incorrect answers in total now end the security check (previously three)."
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.1",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: PTP; meaning: Promise to pay booked; used when: at least one promise booked"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.2",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: PIF; meaning: Already paid; used when: customer says it is paid (all products, if several)"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.3",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: TRA; meaning: Transferred - Arrangements; used when: repayment plan / reduced payments / payment holiday"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.4",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: TCC; meaning: Transferred - Customer Care; used when: hardship, transfer accepted"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.5",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: TCT; meaning: Transferred - Contact Centre; used when: customer insists on a person"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.6",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: NRF; meaning: No promise - refused; used when: attempts used up, or does not want to talk"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.7",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: NHS; meaning: No promise - hardship; used when: hardship, transfer declined"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.8",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: NDS; meaning: No promise - disputed; used when: customer disputes the debt"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.9",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: NSE; meaning: No promise - system error; used when: promise could not be booked after retry"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.10",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: IDF; meaning: Security failed; used when: too many incorrect answers"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.11",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: IDD; meaning: Security declined; used when: customer refuses security"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.12",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: CBK; meaning: Callback booked; used when: third party, callback booked"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.13",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: NCB; meaning: No suitable callback time; used when: third party, no time inside the window"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.14",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: WRN; meaning: Wrong number; used when: number not the customer's"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.15",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: DEC; meaning: Deceased; used when: customer has died"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.16",
   "text": "tool: close_call; code: UNC; meaning: Could not confirm; used when: still unclear who answered after the second ask"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.17",
   "text": "tool: add_note; code: N-REF; meaning: Refused; used when: no promise on this product, refused"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.18",
   "text": "tool: add_note; code: N-HRD; meaning: Hardship; used when: hardship stated on this product"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.19",
   "text": "tool: add_note; code: N-DSP; meaning: Disputed; used when: customer disputes this product"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.20",
   "text": "tool: add_note; code: N-PAID; meaning: Already paid; used when: customer says this product is paid"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.codes.21",
   "text": "tool: add_note; code: N-ERR; meaning: System error; used when: promise for this product failed twice"
  },
  {
   "id": "04-codes.mapping.1",
   "text": "no-promise close for several products: N-REF->NRF, N-HRD->NHS, N-DSP->NDS, N-ERR->NSE"
  }
 ],
