<file path="build-the-builder-v3/build-the-builder/policies/S4.policy.json">
{
 "source": {
  "briefs": [
   "brightwater-collections-notes.md"
  ],
  "overrides_applied": [
   "ID failure threshold: three -> four wrong answers in total. Quote: \"~~three wrong answers in total and it's over~~ → **four** wrong answers in total (any mix of the two questions) and it's over\"",
   "New rule added on 9 Oct: when the past-due total is over three thousand euros, the customer is handed to senior collections and no collection is attempted. Quote: \"**BIG BALANCE RULE (new, agreed 9 Oct):** if the past-due amounts of all products added together come to more than three thousand euros, do not try to collect at all.\"",
   "Holiday moved: All Saints (Sunday 2026-11-01) -> Monday 2026-11-02. Quote: \"All Saints, which falls on a Sunday this year so we take Monday the 2nd of November off instead\"",
   "Holiday moved: St Stephen's Day (Saturday 2026-12-26) -> Monday 2026-12-28. Quote: \"St Stephen's Day, which is a Saturday this year so it moves to Monday 28 December\""
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Single document. Status: \"agreed in the 9 Oct meeting except where marked. Where a line is struck through it was replaced in that meeting, use the replacement.\"",
   "The tool API summary already says four wrong answers, which matches the corrected rule.",
   "<!-- TODO(TO): check with legal if \"specialist\" wording is ok for big balance rule -->"
  ],
  "api_servers": [
   "https://brightwater-mock.example/v0"
  ]
 },
 "variables": [
  {
   "name": "cust_ref",
   "meaning": "the customer id; it goes into `customer_id` on EVERY tool call"
  },
  {
   "name": "first_name",
   "meaning": "customer's first name"
  },
  {
   "name": "surname",
   "meaning": "customer's surname"
  },
  {
   "name": "honorific",
   "meaning": "honorific (Mr / Mrs / Ms / Dr)"
  },
  {
   "name": "now_local",
   "meaning": "the date+time *right now* in the form `DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM` (e.g. `21/10/2026 14:05`). use this for all date stuff, never the server clock!!"
  }
 ],
 "clock": {
  "now_variable": "now_local",
  "timezone": null,
  "date_format": "DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM",
  "notes": [
   "use this for all date stuff, never the server clock!!",
   "The documents do not state a timezone."
  ]
 },
 "calendar": {
  "weekend": [
   6,
   7
  ],
  "holidays": [
   "2026-11-02",
   "2026-12-03",
   "2026-12-25",
   "2026-12-28",
   "2027-01-01"
  ],
  "roll_rule": "next_business_day",
  "week_starts": 1,
  "non_holidays": [
   "2026-12-08"
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Weekends are not working days, obviously. Besides those we're closed on: All Saints, which falls on a Sunday this year so we take Monday the 2nd of November off instead; the staff training day on Thursday 3 December; Christmas Day (Friday) plus St Stephen's Day, which is a Saturday this year so it moves to Monday 28 December; and New Year's Day 2027. (Someone asked about 8 December — no, we are open that day this year.)",
   "weekend / closed day, but before the deadline → offer the next working day after it",
   "The documents do not say which day the calendar week starts on."
  ]
 },
 "opening": {
  "text": "Good day, you're speaking with the Brightwater Mutual call assistant; this call is being recorded.",
  "disclosures": [
   "you're speaking with the Brightwater Mutual call assistant",
   "this call is being recorded"
  ],
  "forbidden_before_verification": [
   "money",
   "arrears",
   "late",
   "owe",
   "debt",
   "any product"
  ],
  "notes": [
   "and DON'T mention money, \"arrears\", \"late\", \"owe\", \"debt\" or any product until they've passed ID. Same for whoever picks up.",
   "then: \"Could I speak with {honorific} {surname}, please?\"",
   "yes / speaking / it's me / their own name = ok",
   "anything else -> ask once more. still not clear -> close **no_contact / unclear**",
   "if they asked something first, answer it, and the next ask is the 2nd ask",
   "\"are you a robot?\" -> say it's Brightwater Mutual's call assistant, carry on.",
   "\"is this a scam?\" -> tell them to ring the number printed on their statement to check. carry on."
  ]
 },
 "third_party": {
  "cases": [
   {
    "trigger": "answer to 'Could I speak with {honorific} {surname}, please?' is not clear after it has been asked twice",
    "say": null,
    "action": "end",
    "outcome": "no_contact",
    "reason": "unclear"
   },
   {
    "trigger": "wrong person picks up and a callback inside the allowed window is agreed",
    "say": null,
    "action": "callback",
    "outcome": "no_contact",
    "reason": "callback"
   },
   {
    "trigger": "wrong person picks up and the second callback time offered is also outside the window",
    "say": null,
    "action": "end",
    "outcome": "no_contact",
    "reason": "no_callback"
   },
   {
    "trigger": "not their number",
    "say": null,
    "action": "end",
    "outcome": "no_contact",
    "reason": "wrong_number"
   },
   {
    "trigger": "customer died",
    "say": "I'm very sorry for your loss.",
    "action": "end",
    "outcome": "no_contact",
    "reason": "deceased"
   }
  ],
  "rules": [
   "never say why we're calling. Ask when {first_name} is around.",
   "customer died → \"I'm very sorry for your loss.\" nothing else, close **no_contact / deceased**",
   "nobody else may do the ID questions, hear about the account or pay for them."
  ],
  "notes": []
 },
 "identity": {
  "questions": [
   {
    "order": 1,
    "tool_field": "date_of_birth",
    "ask": "date of birth",
    "answer_format": "date",
    "normalise": "dmy_to_iso",
    "tool_format": "YYYY-MM-DD"
   },
   {
    "order": 2,
    "tool_field": "national_id_last3",
    "ask": "the last three digits of their national ID number",
    "answer_format": "digits",
    "normalise": "digits_only",
    "tool_format": "three digits"
   }
  ],
  "max_wrong": 4,
  "max_wrong_scope": "total",
  "wrong_counts_rules": [
   "**four** wrong answers in total (any mix of the two questions) and it's over",
   "numbers-only dates are day/month/year",
   "Tool API: unreadable dates are rejected with ok=false and not counted.",
   "Tool API: the verify_identity response includes wrong_answers_left."
  ],
  "fail": {
   "outcome": "id_fail",
   "reason": "failed",
   "say": "say nothing about the account, point them to online banking or a branch"
  },
  "notes": [
   "two questions, one at a time",
   "won't answer → explain once it protects them. Refuses again (or keeps asking what it's about) → **id_fail / declined**.",
   "\"I don't want to talk\" ×2 before ID → id_fail / declined",
   "get_account is refused until both questions are passed."
  ]
 },
 "products": {
  "max_count": 3,
  "types": {
   "credit_card": {
    "speak_as": "your credit card ending {card_last4}",
    "floor_field": "minimum_payment",
    "floor_expr": null,
    "full_field": "past_due"
   },
   "loan": {
    "speak_as": "your loan",
    "floor_field": "instalment_amount",
    "floor_expr": null,
    "full_field": "past_due"
   },
   "overdraft": {
    "speak_as": "your overdraft",
    "floor_field": null,
    "floor_expr": "min(50, past_due)",
    "full_field": "past_due"
   }
  },
  "order": "as_returned",
  "list_field": "products",
  "type_field": "type",
  "id_field": "product_id",
  "days_late_field": "days_late",
  "notes": [
   "Say we're calling from Brightwater's payments team about overdue amounts. One sentence per product: \"your credit card ending 1234\" / \"your loan\" / \"your overdraft\", how much is past due, how many days late. ALL products before asking anything.",
   "**BIG BALANCE RULE (new, agreed 9 Oct):** if the past-due amounts of all products added together come to more than three thousand euros, do not try to collect at all. After stating the products, tell the customer a specialist will help them, call `transfer_to_agent` with queue `senior_collections` and close **handed_over / high_balance**. Exactly three thousand is not \"more than\".",
